NOTICE
======

LICENSE covers this repository's own contents: the build scripts, the Makefiles, the kernel config fragment,
the workflows and the docs. Nothing upstream is vendored here; every dependency is fetched at build time.

This file covers the ARTIFACTS the repository publishes, namely the installer image
(ghcr.io/yama6a/talos-raspberry-pi5) and the raw disk image (metal-arm64-rpi5.raw.xz). Those are an aggregate
of separately licensed works, and each keeps its own license.


Components of the published artifacts
-------------------------------------

  Linux kernel                 GPL-2.0-only
    Source:  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux at the commit named in the release's build-inputs.json
    Patches: https://github.com/siderolabs/pkgs at the commit named there, kernel/build/patches/
             minus the entries in kernel/patch-skip.txt of this repository
    Config:  siderolabs/pkgs kernel/build/config-arm64, plus kernel/pi5-rpi.fragment of this repository,
             reconciled by `make olddefconfig`. Both halves ship as release assets
             (kernel-config-arm64.base and kernel-config-arm64.fragment).

  U-Boot                       GPL-2.0-or-later
    Source:  https://github.com/talos-rpi5/u-boot at the tag pinned by talos-rpi5/sbc-raspberrypi5

  Device trees and overlays    GPL-2.0 OR MIT
    Source:  https://github.com/raspberrypi/linux (bcm2712*.dtb) and
             https://github.com/raspberrypi/firmware (boot/overlays/*.dtbo)

  Talos Linux                  MPL-2.0   https://github.com/siderolabs/talos
  Talos pkgs                   MPL-2.0   https://github.com/siderolabs/pkgs
  Raspberry Pi 5 overlay       MPL-2.0   https://github.com/talos-rpi5/sbc-raspberrypi5
  iscsi-tools extension        MPL-2.0   https://github.com/siderolabs/extensions
  util-linux-tools extension   MPL-2.0   https://github.com/siderolabs/extensions

The image's EFI partition additionally carries COPYING.linux (the GPL-2.0 text) and LICENCE.broadcom, both
placed there by the overlay. No proprietary Broadcom firmware is shipped: the Pi 5's second-stage bootloader
lives in on-board SPI EEPROM, so an image for it needs no start*.elf or fixup*.dat.


Source for the GPL-licensed parts
---------------------------------

Offered under GPL-2.0 section 3(a): the complete corresponding source is public and pinned exactly.

Every release carries a build-inputs.json asset naming the precise upstream commit of each source, and an
SPDX SBOM declaring the kernel GPL-2.0-only. Together with this repository at the release's git tag, that is
everything needed to reproduce the binaries:

    git clone --branch <release-tag> https://github.com/yama6a/talos-raspberry-pi5
    cd talos-raspberry-pi5 && make build

Reproducing requires network access to the upstream repositories above. The archives are not mirrored here.
If an upstream ref named in a build-inputs.json ever becomes unreachable, open an issue on this repository.
